  "why": "The repository's depth-chart join covered 4 of 32 clubs (KC, GB, NE, DET) and resolved chains for 2 (LAR, SEA). Suggestions S-33 and S-39 and question Q-37 name the 32-club transcription as the blocking data task. This file adds six clubs whose charts were read live today, so the join covers 10 of 32.",
  "string_rule": "Depth string = the position of a player's name in his club's row, counting from the club's own left-hand (1st string) entry. A club that prints two names in one cell has both recorded at that slot; a club that prints a hole (WAS LB2 middle cell) keeps the hole, so the player after it is 3rd string, which is what the club published.",
  "best_slot_rule": "Where a club lists one player at more than one slot, the shallowest slot is used as his string and the duplicate is recorded in also_listed_at. A player absent from his club's chart has string = not published, never a guess.",
  "official_status": "Unofficial. Every club labels these charts 'Unofficial'. They are the club's own published document and the only club-level depth source that exists: nfl.com's own /team/depth-chart route returns 404 (verified by an earlier session). They are not the game-day active list.",
  "sources": "One https:// URL per club, recorded under charts.<club>.url. The chart's own printed date is recorded where the club prints one; several clubs print none, and that cell stays 'not published'."
